# Concrete products, shared internals

**Kumkaj** is the **brand** for a family of **concrete business operating system apps**. **Current focus: Kumkaj Courier** (`docs/KUMKAJ_COURIER.md`) — full courier-agency BOS. Other concrete products come later. Internally we share reusable code and extract more when a second product needs the same thing.

Canonical product text: `docs/KUMKAJ_PRODUCT_VISION_AND_REQUIREMENTS.md` §1–2 and §31–33; courier brief: `docs/KUMKAJ_COURIER.md`.

## Do

- Ship concrete product UX first (labels, flows, packaging, defaults).
- Prefer shapes that can become shared: party, item/line, unit, charge, ledger, day book, report view, document template.
- When a second product needs the same logic, move it into shared code.
- Hide unused capability inside each product; progressive depth per product.

## Do not

- Maintain forever-divergent engines / duplicated ledgers per trade.
- Add throwaway vertical schemas that cannot be extracted (`CourierShipment` as a second books stack).
- Force one vague “works for anyone” UI that the owner must reinterpret.

```text
❌ Five forked apps with five day books
✅ Concrete “Courier” / “Counter” / “Personal” products + shared books primitives
```
